1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,000
After being rescued from slavery and
brought to the edge of the Promised Land,

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
God's people feared the enemies before
them,

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
instead of trusting the victory God had
promised.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
So God sent his people back into the
wilderness.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
There, a rebellion rose against Moses'
leadership.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Consequences struck, the earth opened,
fire fell, and plagues spread.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
But Aaron and Moses interceded for the
rebellious people,

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
and the Lord showed mercy.

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Now, the journey continues in a dry land

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
where God's people surround Moses to ask
for water.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Welcome to Mariners Church. My name is
Jared.

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
I'm so excited to be with you today.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Before we jump into today's message,

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
I want to take one final moment before we
close out our ministry year.

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000
We have the unique blessing of getting to
hear your stories every single week

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
about how God has saved you. He has
restored your marriage.

17
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
He's provided for you in a time of need.

18
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,000
We hear stories of healings.

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
The glory of the Lord is constantly on
display.

20
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Your heart is what we care about the most.

21
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
We have all kinds of ministries and
programs and groups and studies and teachings.

22
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
We have so many things at the church.

23
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
All of them are here to help you grow
closer to God,

24
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
and I hope you take advantage. I hope you
lean in.

25
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
But I don't want you to miss one
significant area

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
in which God has access to your heart.

27
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Money has a unique grip on us,

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
and it's through regular giving to the
church,

29
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,000
which is a primary way in which God can
form us

30
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
into a person more like Jesus.

31
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
That's what I want for my life.

32
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
It's what I want for my family, and it's
what I want for you.

33
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
So if you're ready to jump into recurring
giving,

34
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
I want to invite you to do so.

35
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:54,000
I'm so grateful for those of you that
already do.

36
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:59,000
You are a part of the work that God is
doing all around us here at Mariners Church.

37
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
If you want to jump in, you can text
online to the number on the screen.

38
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Follow those prompts, and you will be set
up.

39
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
All right, let's get into today's message.

40
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:15,000
I want you to imagine a 10-year-old on a
two-week road trip with his parents.

41
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
So you're in a 1988 Suburban, no air
conditioning.

42
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
You start in Los Angeles.

43
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
You head east to Branson, Missouri, which
is the Disneyland for the retirement community.

44
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
You then travel up north into Michigan

45
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
and you make your way back west all the
way to Seattle

46
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
and then you drive back down to home in
L.A.

47
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:39,000
That is about 88 hours of continuous
driving over a two-week period.

48
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:46,000
It's 6,000 miles, and that was the most
extravagant vacation of my entire childhood.

49
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
We had these big adventures of going to
antique stores

50
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:52,000
in which I collected baseball cards I no
longer have.

51
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
And the saddest part is iPads weren't even
invented yet.

52
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
It was the longest two weeks of my life.

53
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Now can you imagine doing that with kids
today with no devices?

54
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Just in the car, locked in together for
weeks on end.

55
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
I can't even make it to L.A., the starting
point,

56
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,000
without my kids asking how much longer and
do we have snacks and stop hitting me.

57
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
I mean, cars are chaos with kids.

58
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
I don't care if it's 10 minutes or 10
hours.

59
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
It's just like, end the misery.

60
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:29,000
Okay, we're picking up on the story here
of the people of God in Numbers,

61
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,000
and it's a narrative.

62
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
We've been watching a story unfold from
where we began just a few weeks ago

63
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
to where our story is going to pick up
today.

64
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
The people of God have been nomadic.

65
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,000
They have been on the move for 38 years.

66
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
far longer than my two-week road trip.

67
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Let's pick up our story today in Numbers
chapter 20.

68
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:54,000
We're going to start in verse 1.

69
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:59,000
The entire Israelite community entered the
wilderness of Zin in the first month

70
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
and they settled in Kadesh.

71
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Miriam died and was buried there.

72
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
So the opening verse gives us the context
of both the location

73
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
but also what is happening inside of this
family.

74
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Kadesh is 200 miles north of Egypt.

75
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Let me show you a map here so you can kind
of get an understanding

76
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:23,000
of where Egypt is in relation to where now
Israel is, modern-day Israel.

77
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Kadesh is sort of right there in the
center,

78
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
and they're on their way towards the
promised land,

79
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
which is a region known as Canaan.

80
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Now this is the exact location, Kadesh is,

81
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
where our message from two weeks ago took
place.

82
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Remember when Eric taught us about the 12
tribes

83
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
encamped in a place called Kadesh,

84
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
and they elected two scouts from each
tribe.

85
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
They were sent into the region called
Canaan,

86
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
which is this promised land by God.

87
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
But they came back, and they reported of
these giants in the land.

88
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
They allowed their fear to take over.

89
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:04,000
They expressed a lack of trust in God, and
they faced a severe consequence.

90
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Because of their lack of trust in that
story,

91
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:13,000
40 years is going to be spent following
God in the wilderness.

92
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Now, I almost tripped up on my words.

93
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
I don't know if you caught me, but I think
about this as like,

94
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,000
I always think like they were wandering in
the wilderness for 40 years.

95
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
But it's not actually wandering.

96
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
God is the one who was leading them.

97
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Remember, it was a pillar of smoke by day
and fire by night.

98
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Anytime God moved, the people would
follow.

99
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:38,000
God led them throughout the entirety of a
generation in the wilderness.

100
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
You see, God wanted them.

101
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Because of this consequence of their lack
of trust,

102
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:49,000
God had them following him until this
unbelieving generation all had died.

103
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Now, Miriam, who is Moses' sister,

104
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:56,000
her death proves that there was going to
be no special exceptions,

105
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
not even for Moses' family.

106
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
But the consequence was for them as well.

107
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
So the story continues in verse 2.

108
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
It says,

109
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:36,000
So the people of God are frustrated.

110
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
And it kind of sounds like they want a
charcuterie board.

111
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
But there's real pain that's inside of
this for them.

112
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,000
You see, the children of this prior
generation are now standing

113
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
in the same location as the first
rebellion.

114
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:53,000
This place, Kadesh, is the same place in
which those scouts were sent.

115
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,000
And what is happening?

116
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:59,000
The children of them, the ones who were
grumbling back then,

117
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
now the children are doing the same.

118
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
But there is something real that they're
complaining about.

119
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
They're saying, we have no water.

120
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
And you and I know that three days without
water would be death.

121
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
This was a real issue.

122
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Their complaint, though, is almost word
for word

123
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,000
what their parents said decades ago.

124
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
That story in Exodus chapter 17.

125
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
They say, why did you bring us out of
Egypt to die here?

126
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Now notice who they were quarreling with.

127
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
It wasn't with each other.

128
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,000
It wasn't actually God.

129
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
They were quarreling with Moses.

130
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
You see, the people following after Moses,

131
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:40,000
they confused Moses to be their provider,
not their leader.

132
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,000
That's going to be a really important
point here.

133
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,000
But Moses is kind of an important figure.

134
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Maybe you can remember.

135
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Moses was raised in the house of Pharaoh.

136
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,000
He was chosen by God to lead his people
out of the Exodus.

137
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:57,000
You have the amazing stories of the
plagues and the splitting of the Red Sea.

138
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:00,000
He is the one who provided the Ten
Commandments.

139
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
God gave them to him, and he descended
down the mountain to give them.

140
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,000
This was God's guy.

141
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Throughout the whole Old Testament,

142
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:13,000
you see God in search of a human to
partner with.

143
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
His first creation, Adam.

144
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Then we carry on to the stories of
Abraham.

145
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
And now we see Moses.

146
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
There are others along the way.

147
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
And guess what?

148
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,000
There's going to be others to follow.

149
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:30,000
God wants to partner with someone in order
to repair what we had broken.

150
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
So then the story goes on.

151
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
So the people are complaining.

152
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
They go to Moses, and they say,

153
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,000
We need water.

154
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
So what does Moses and Aaron do?

155
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Here's verse 6.

156
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Then Moses and Aaron went from the
presence of the assembly

157
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
to the doorway of the tent of meeting,
which is the tabernacle.

158
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
That's where God's presence was.

159
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:54,000
They fell face down, and all the glory of
the Lord appeared to them.

160
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
The Lord spoke to Moses,

161
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Take the staff and assemble the community.

162
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:02,000
You and your brother Aaron are to speak to
the rock while they watch,

163
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
and it will yield its water.

164
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
You will bring out water for them from the
rock

165
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
and provide drink for the community and
their livestock.

166
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,000
So Moses took the staff from the Lord's
presence

167
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
just as he had commanded them.

168
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
Now, they did the right thing.

169
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Moses and Aaron, they went to God.

170
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
They bowed down before him,

171
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
and they knew that God is the one who is
ultimately going to provide.

172
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
He is the great provider.

173
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
He is the sustainer of their life in the
wilderness.

174
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
He has been providing for them for
decades,

175
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
a generation at this point.

176
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
So Moses takes the complaint to the only
place

177
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
where complaints belong, to the tent of
meeting,

178
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:45,000
which is the tabernacle, the very presence
of God.

179
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
God gives them instructions.

180
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
He tells them exactly what to do.

181
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
And then here's verse 10.

182
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Moses and Aaron summoned the assembly in
front of the rock,

183
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
and Moses said to them, Listen, you
rebels,

184
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,000
must we bring water out of this rock for
you?

185
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Then Moses raised his hand,

186
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
and he struck the rock twice with his
staff,

187
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
so that an abundant water gushed out,

188
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
and the community and their livestock
drank.

189
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Wow.

190
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
I mean, it is a miracle.

191
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
This is a miracle what has happened,

192
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
but did you catch the problem?

193
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,000
You see, this miracle is God providing.

194
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
They're at this point, there are millions
of people.

195
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
This is not a little stream flows out of a
rock.

196
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
This is an abundant river that can provide
for the people

197
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
and for all of their livestock.

198
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Why is it that God did that?

199
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Why did he choose even though something
was wrong in the story?

200
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:43,000
You see, God was not appeasing the crowd.

201
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,000
This is God providing for his people.

202
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,000
But a plot twist is about to happen.

203
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Look what happens in verse 12.

204
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
But the Lord said to Moses and Aaron,

205
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Because you did not trust me to
demonstrate my holiness

206
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:58,000
in the sight of the Israelites,

207
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:03,000
you will not bring this assembly into the
land I have given them.

208
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,000
These are the waters of Meribah,

209
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:08,000
where the Israelites quarreled with the
Lord,

210
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:11,000
and he demonstrated his holiness to them.

211
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Okay, you're probably like, wait a second.

212
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
I've heard this story before.

213
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
I don't really remember it ending in that
way.

214
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
And you're absolutely right.

215
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
This is a parallel story.

216
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
You see, Numbers chapter 20, the story we
just read,

217
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:30,000
is a very similar story to what had
happened years prior,

218
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,000
taking place in Exodus chapter 17.

219
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:36,000
In fact, let me show you the parallel of
these stories.

220
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,000
You see that God gives instructions in
Exodus 17,

221
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,000
the other story.

222
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
He says, strike the rock.

223
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
And so what is Moses' action?

224
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
He strikes the rock.

225
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
And then what is God's response when that
happens?

226
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Water flows.

227
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
That's probably the story you remember,

228
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
but that's not the story we just read.

229
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Let me show you what happens in Numbers
chapter 20.

230
00:11:56,000 --> 00:12:00,000
God says, speak to the rock.

231
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
What was Moses' action?

232
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,000
He strikes the rock.

233
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
So then what is God's response?

234
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:12,000
He prohibits Moses and Aaron from entering
the promised land.

235
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,000
And yet there is one other response from
God.

236
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:19,000
The water still flows.

237
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,000
You see, God in Numbers chapter 20, he
said,

238
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:26,000
take your staff, but don't use it.

239
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
He says to speak to the rock.

240
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Don't strike the rock.

241
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
In Exodus chapter 17, God told him to
strike the rock,

242
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
and then water came out.

243
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
It was the same problem that they were
facing.

244
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:41,000
They needed water in both stories.

245
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:43,000
In fact, it was the same person.

246
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Moses was the one.

247
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
And Moses had the same staff.

248
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
God said, take your staff.

249
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
But then he gave him a different command.

250
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
He said, speak to the rock.

251
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Don't actually use your staff.

252
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
This staff is kind of an incredible thing.

253
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:03,000
It's the same staff that turned the Nile
River into blood in the Exodus story.

254
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:05,000
It's the one that parted the Red Sea.

255
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:09,000
It's the one that prior had struck the
rock and water flowed.

256
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
But God said, take it.

257
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Don't use it.

258
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:17,000
You see, sometimes obedience for you and I
means picking up that tool

259
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
or that thing that we're known for,

260
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:24,000
but then also setting it back down because
God said something different.

261
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
It means surrendering to God and
remembering that the staff,

262
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
and this is good for you and I to
remember,

263
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:34,000
that the staff was only ever as powerful
as God allowed it to be.

264
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:38,000
God's instructions changed, and Moses
missed it.

265
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Well, he either missed it or he
disregarded it.

266
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Now, we've probably all been in a place
where you've experienced, like,

267
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:48,000
what got you here won't get you there.

268
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
We learn things in our life.

269
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:55,000
We find ways to do the things that we
enjoy or the discipline that we need.

270
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
But sometimes those things hit a ceiling,

271
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
and what got us here isn't what's going to
get us there.

272
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:04,000
This came so real for me as I started
raising children.

273
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:08,000
If you have kids, you know that each phase
of a child's development

274
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
requires a different style of parenting.

275
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:14,000
What you did when they were infants is not
what you can do when they're toddlers,

276
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
and it's definitely different than when
they become teenagers.

277
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Now, the total plot twist is that you
could have two kids in the same age group,

278
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:26,000
and it still requires two different
approaches to parenting.

279
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:31,000
What got you to one child is not the same
for the next child.

280
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Now, I have two kids. I very much
experienced this in my own home.

281
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:39,000
My firstborn, my son, Asher, when he was
told to go to his room,

282
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
when he was, like, five, six, seven years
old,

283
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:44,000
when he was told to go to his room, he
would storm down the hall,

284
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:48,000
and then he would kind of politely close
his door, and then he'd sit on his bed,

285
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
and about 30 seconds later, you'd hear his
sweet little voice go,

286
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Can I come out now?

287
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:57,000
Well, then as my daughter got into that
age group, and we told her to go to her room,

288
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
she said, No.

289
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
And so we told her again, Go to your room,
and she said, No.

290
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
And so we had to pick her up and put her
in her room,

291
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:10,000
and then she would yank on that door like
a little personal tornado inside that room.

292
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
It was crazy, the differences of our kid.

293
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:20,000
You see, we had to operate differently
even in the same children in our own house.

294
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Moses experienced this.

295
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:29,000
You see, what worked once for Moses was
not going to work again.

296
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:33,000
You may be asking why this is such a grave
offense.

297
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
It's a pretty big consequence that Moses
faced,

298
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
but you've got to understand from God's
perspective.

299
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Moses put himself in the place of God.

300
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:47,000
There's a pastor and writer that I love
named Tim Keller, and he said this.

301
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:53,000
He says that when Moses calls them rebels,
Moses sets himself up as their judge.

302
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
He condemned them.

303
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,000
And then in saying, Must we bring you
water?

304
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:01,000
He sets them up as their deliverer.

305
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Everything Moses did pointed away from God
and actually to himself.

306
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:12,000
So just as the people confused Moses to be
their provider and not their leader,

307
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Moses was confused as well.

308
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Moses actually believed it, too.

309
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:23,000
So if Moses' consequence was a plot twist,
like if you didn't see that coming,

310
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
the other one is that water came out
anyway.

311
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Like, Moses did the wrong thing.

312
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Moses faced a consequence, and yet God
still provided for the people,

313
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
even when his servant disobeyed.

314
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:40,000
You see, there's this whole generation
that God desires to preserve.

315
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
This is kind of dangerous territory if you
think about it.

316
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:48,000
Just because something works doesn't mean
that God blesses it.

317
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:53,000
The water flowed and yet the leader,
Moses, he still got disqualified.

318
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Results are not the same as obedience.

319
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,000
You see, the wilderness was not ever
really the problem,

320
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
it's the heart.

321
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
The problem is not we're short on water,

322
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:11,000
the problem really in this story is who's
gonna get the glory when the water flows out.

323
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Now, I shared with you two different
stories.

324
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:17,000
There's the parallel of Exodus 17 and
Numbers chapter 20.

325
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,000
It's two different locations,

326
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:24,000
and yet, did you notice the name Waters of
Meribah being used?

327
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:27,000
The Waters of Meribah is a really specific
name.

328
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:34,000
In fact, it's a name that was given by
Moses at the end of the story in Exodus chapter 17.

329
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Moses names the location Meribah, which
means quarreling or complaining or bitterness

330
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
because that's exactly how the people were
acting.

331
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:49,000
So Moses names the place in Exodus 17
Meribah.

332
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:56,000
But did you notice that in Numbers chapter
20, it's a different location, and yet it's the same water?

333
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:03,000
The location in which they're at is called
Kadesh,

334
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:10,000
which means holy or set apart or sacred
but now it is called the waters of Meribah because of Moses' quarreling with the people.

335
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Two different locations, two different
fights, but bitterness ensues.

336
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:22,000
You see, God's name is supposed to be holy
in the place called holy, Kadesh,

337
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:27,000
but Moses gave its bitter name instead.

338
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Now this is a big deal for God.

339
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Holiness is not God being sensitive or
touchy.

340
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Holiness is God being God.

341
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:43,000
And so to treat a holy God casually is to
misrepresent him to the people who need to know exactly who he is.

342
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Moses misrepresented God to the very
people God was trying to reach.

343
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:57,000
Now, the relationship between God and
Moses is so important and so fascinating.

344
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,000
If you're right now enjoying the World Cup
like I am,

345
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:05,000
you probably are watching some of the
commentating that is happening as well.

346
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:09,000
I love soccer. I've been a soccer fan for
many, many years now.

347
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:13,000
And so you know that Zlatan is a part of
the commentating staff right now.

348
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
And this guy is a global pillar in soccer.

349
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
Like the world knows who Zlatan is.

350
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:22,000
But he's sharing a desk with another guy
named Lexi Lawless.

351
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
And Lexi's a former U.S. player.

352
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:29,000
And I don't mean that in a demeaning way,
but he's not Zlatan, okay?

353
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
Zlatan is like a powerhouse,

354
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,000
and then you've got Lexi, who has played
soccer. It's wonderful.

355
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
In fact, they both played in the MLS,
which is an important part of the detail here.

356
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
But every now and then, you watch Lexi
think he's friends with Zlatan.

357
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:46,000
He tries to jab him. He tries to kind of
rib him a little bit.

358
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:50,000
He tries to play jokes on Zlatan,

359
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
and that's where you can see the
difference between the two.

360
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Zlatan has nothing to do with it.

361
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:58,000
I mean, his separation from Lexi is some
of the best nighttime television going on right now.

362
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Here's what happened. They both played for
the MLS back in the day.

363
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Zlatan, while he played for some of the
world's greatest clubs, he finished his career right here on the LA Galaxy.

364
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Zlatan, while he played for some of the
world's greatest clubs,

365
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:15,000
he finished his career right here on the
L.A. Galaxy.

366
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:20,000
And Zlatan's ego is so big that when he
committed to the L.A. Galaxy,

367
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,000
they took an ad out in the L.A. Times.

368
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:28,000
In fact, you can see right here in this
image, the cover page is him in his Galaxy jersey.

369
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:34,000
But more importantly, Zlatan himself
wanted the back cover all to himself.

370
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:39,000
And the text reads just simply, Dear Los
Angeles, you're welcome.

371
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
I love it. I love it so much.

372
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Zlatan and Lexi are not on the same level.

373
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:50,000
They might share a desk together, but they
are different people.

374
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:55,000
God and Moses exponentially further apart.

375
00:20:55,000 --> 00:21:02,000
God will not stand for Moses taking credit
or reducing God's holiness.

376
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,000
Now, in the grand scheme of where we've
been in the book of Numbers,

377
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:10,000
this is now the third of three rebellions.

378
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:15,000
These rebellions each have deepening
consequences, and it's a triplet.

379
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:20,000
And in fact, you have maybe noticed
throughout Scripture that anytime something comes in threes,

380
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:22,000
it's like an exclamation point.

381
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:27,000
When God is called Holy, Holy, Holy,
that's meant to be an exclamation point.

382
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,000
And in these rebellions, it's like a
spiral.

383
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:32,000
Each rebellion is getting more severe.

384
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Let me show you the graphic that we saw
from week one.

385
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:40,000
You can see here the 12 tribes, as
instructed in the book of Numbers,

386
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,000
are encamped around the tabernacle.

387
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Right inside between the tribes and the
tabernacle themselves is the Levitical tribe.

388
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,000
We learned about them last week.

389
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
And at the center is the tabernacle
itself.

390
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
That is the dwelling place of God.

391
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:58,000
The three rebellions follow these three
concentric circles.

392
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:03,000
Numbers chapter 13, after traveling 200
miles north from Egypt,

393
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,000
the scouts are sent out.

394
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:05,000
They come back.

395
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,000
They are terrified.

396
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Their fear and their lack of trust
resulted in 40 years of the wilderness.

397
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:12,000
That's the outside circle.

398
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:15,000
Then last week, we saw Korah.

399
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:20,000
We saw in Numbers chapter 16 that Korah
rose up against Moses and Aaron.

400
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:25,000
His own pride and jealousy took over, and
the ground swallowed up.

401
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:28,000
In fact, if you missed that message,
you've got to go back to last week.

402
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,000
Eric's message was amazing.

403
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:31,000
I want you to hear that.

404
00:22:31,000 --> 00:22:34,000
And now the third rebellion, the inner
circle,

405
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,000
in the exact same location as the first
rebellion,

406
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:40,000
we are now here at the tabernacle.

407
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:43,000
These are God's guys, Moses and Aaron.

408
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,000
40 years they've led people through the
wilderness,

409
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:49,000
and they have arrived back exactly where
it started.

410
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:56,000
But this time, we see that the inner
circle is susceptible to failure too.

411
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
They're so close to the promised land.

412
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
In fact, look at this map.

413
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Kadesh is on the border of Canaan, the
promised land,

414
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
the place in which they're trying to go.

415
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
They traveled 200 miles,

416
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:13,000
and they're only 80 miles away from being
in the place in which God promised to them.

417
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:18,000
And this is the place that Moses was
disqualified.

418
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:22,000
He was prohibited from entering into the
promised land.

419
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
And you might be asking yourself,

420
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,000
like, isn't that kind of harsh?

421
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,000
Like, does this feel too harsh?

422
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:30,000
I don't know.

423
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Let me tell you about how harsh I can be
sometimes.

424
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:36,000
I recently got the worst haircut of my
life.

425
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
And I know what you're probably thinking,

426
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
and it kind of hurts because it isn't this
haircut, okay?

427
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,000
It's not this one.

428
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,000
It was a prior one.

429
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
But I sat down in the chair to a guy that
I'd never seen before,

430
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
and he looks at me and says,

431
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:49,000
all right, what are we doing here today?

432
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:50,000
And I kind of explained it.

433
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:51,000
And he says this.

434
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:54,000
So your hair, like, swoops forward and
then over.

435
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Like, is that what you want?

436
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:01,000
And he said it in such a way that I was
like, no, definitely not.

437
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:03,000
And I said the worst thing you can say to
somebody.

438
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,000
I said, just do whatever you think.

439
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:09,000
And within 10 seconds, I knew that I was
doomed.

440
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:14,000
And I also knew I would never return back
to that guy.

441
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:18,000
You see, Moses, well, for me, that was a
small mistake.

442
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,000
And I will never go back to him.

443
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:21,000
Maybe that's too harsh.

444
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:24,000
But Moses did not make a small mistake.

445
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:27,000
He put himself in the place of God.

446
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:29,000
He made himself the provider.

447
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:33,000
He took the credit for what only God could
do.

448
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Now, I want you to understand that this
was a consequence, not a punishment.

449
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,000
What are the differences there?

450
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,000
And I know I'm going to kind of play with
words here a little bit,

451
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:47,000
but I do think it's important for our own
understanding of God.

452
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:52,000
As I've shared already, God desired a
human partner.

453
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Moses was God's chosen leader from the
plagues to the splitting of the sea,

454
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:57,000
the Ten Commandments.

455
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:03,000
And now in this story, we see that the
mighty are able to fall.

456
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:07,000
There's a book that Jim Collins wrote in
2009 called

457
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,000
How the Mighty Fall.

458
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:10,000
It's easier than some people realize.

459
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:13,000
When building a company, in the pursuit of
more,

460
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:16,000
they start to overreach into what is
waiting for them.

461
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,000
They have moved outside of their core
competence,

462
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:22,000
and they are now operating in a place of
risk.

463
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:26,000
And so when the time comes, there's a
little downturn in their profitability.

464
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:30,000
They start to grasp for salvation, and
that's Jim Collins' words.

465
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:34,000
They start to look for that silver bullet,
the new leader, the bold pivot,

466
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,000
this radical restructure.

467
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,000
And then most fail.

468
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:41,000
They slip into irrelevance or death.

469
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:42,000
And here's his closing point.

470
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:46,000
If leaders can catch decline early enough,
and name it honestly,

471
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:50,000
and they can return to the disciplines
that produced greatness in the first place,

472
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:53,000
rather than reaching for an outside savior
themselves,

473
00:25:53,000 --> 00:25:56,000
they would not fall or fail.

474
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Moses did not catch his decline early
enough.

475
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:03,000
He allowed the pressure and the demands to
bend his actions,

476
00:26:04,000 --> 00:26:06,000
and his consequences feel harsh.

477
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:09,000
But Moses is not an average person.

478
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:11,000
Moses is not like you and I.

479
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:13,000
This is the leader of the people of God.

480
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:17,000
The holiness of God is not something to be
messed with.

481
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:21,000
So God needed a partner, and even Moses
failed.

482
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,000
Even Moses was able to fail.

483
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:29,000
Now, that failure is both an illustration
and an example for us,

484
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:32,000
but it's also a reminder that at the end
of the day,

485
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:35,000
every human was eventually going to fail.

486
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:37,000
And so what does God do?

487
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:42,000
You know, eventually God sent his own son
to be the God-man,

488
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:45,000
fully God, fully man, who would not fail
or fall.

489
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Jesus is the rock, and it is on this
foundation that the church was built.

490
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:53,000
The victory of Jesus is our victory.

491
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:56,000
That the punishment has been satisfied.

492
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,000
The punishment was paid by Jesus.

493
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:00,000
The wrath was poured out on him.

494
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:03,000
We are human, and we fail too.

495
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:09,000
And our failure is not final, and our
punishment has already been paid.

496
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:11,000
That is the grace of Jesus.

497
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:14,000
That is the beauty of having a
relationship with him.

498
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:18,000
While we may fail, and there may be
consequences for our actions,

499
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:24,000
we will not face punishment because Jesus
has on our behalf.

500
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Now, you're probably thinking, wasn't this
story all about people being thirsty?

501
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,000
And the answer is yes.

502
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:36,000
And inevitably, only Jesus, who is the
rock, can be the provider of living water.

503
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:41,000
There's one story in the New Testament, as
Jesus was with his closest 12 disciples.

504
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:43,000
In Matthew chapter 16, it says this.

505
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:48,000
When Jesus came to the region of Caesarea
Philippi, he asked his disciples,

506
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:51,000
who do people say that the Son of Man is?

507
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:55,000
And they replied, some say John the
Baptist, others Elijah, still others Jeremiah,

508
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:57,000
or one of the prophets.

509
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:02,000
But you, he asked them, who do you say I
am?

510
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:07,000
And Simon Peter answered, you are the
Messiah, the Son of the living God.

511
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:10,000
And Jesus responded, blessed are you,
Simon son of Jonah,

512
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:15,000
because flesh and blood did not reveal
this to you, but my Father in heaven.

513
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:20,000
And I also say to you that you are Peter,
and on this rock I will build my church,

514
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:23,000
and the gates of Hades will not overpower
it.

515
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:27,000
And I will give you the keys of the
kingdom of heaven.

516
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Let's contrast these two stories.

517
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Moses at Kadesh, now called Meribah, God
said, speak to the rock,

518
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:39,000
and Moses spoke to the people instead.

519
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:42,000
And what he said was words of bitterness.

520
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:47,000
He said, listen, you rebels, must we bring
water out of this rock for you?

521
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:51,000
And then the verdict came from God,
because you, Moses and Aaron,

522
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:56,000
did not trust me to demonstrate my
holiness in the sight of the Israelites.

523
00:28:56,000 --> 00:29:01,000
You will not bring this assembly into the
land.

524
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:05,000
But Peter at Caesarea Philippi, when Jesus
said, who do you say that I am?

525
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Peter spoke, and he said, on this
confession, he says,

526
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:13,000
you are the Messiah, the son of the living
God.

527
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:17,000
He named Christ correctly in front of the
disciples,

528
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:21,000
in front of this rock, which was filled
with false gods and pagan worship.

529
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:24,000
And then the commission from Jesus came.

530
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:26,000
Jesus says to them, on this rock,

531
00:29:26,000 --> 00:29:30,000
so on the confession that Peter made about
Jesus being the Messiah,

532
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:34,000
I will build my church, and I will give
you the kingdom of heaven.

533
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:37,000
Peter rightly represented God in front of
people,

534
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:41,000
and was given the keys to the kingdom.

535
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:45,000
You see, Moses spoke to the people, and he
faced a consequence.

536
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:49,000
When Jesus was with Peter, Peter said, you
are the Messiah.

537
00:29:49,000 --> 00:29:54,000
And Jesus says, it is on that confession
that I will build the church,

538
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:57,000
the church that you and I are a part of
today,

539
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:01,000
and you will be given the keys of the
kingdom.

540
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:08,000
The contrast is both beautiful, and it is
a warning sign for all of us.

541
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:14,000
You see, it's inside of the wilderness
that rebellions can happen.

542
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:20,000
And I think already you know that if Moses
can fail, so can you and I.

543
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:24,000
And when challenges come, when our needs
go unmet,

544
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:28,000
when the dreams that you have for your
life are met with opposition,

545
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:33,000
this is where we are most susceptible to
rebellion.

546
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:36,000
This is when your perseverance begins to
wane.

547
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:41,000
When your frustration increases, and
hopelessness starts to creep in,

548
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:45,000
and you start to ask yourself, what am I
doing wrong?

549
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:50,000
Why can't I get out of this rut? What's
wrong with me?

550
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:56,000
How long can that frustration go before it
starts to become grumbling?

551
00:30:56,000 --> 00:31:01,000
It's really only a matter of time, if not
carefully managed,

552
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:05,000
that we will begin to grumble, just like
the people of God.

553
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:08,000
That we've seen all throughout the book of
Numbers.

554
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:13,000
You see, their grumbling ultimately
becomes an indictment against God.

555
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:18,000
We would be better off in slavery. You
have brought us here to die.

556
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:23,000
That is what the people of God has
declared throughout the book of Numbers.

557
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:30,000
So let me ask you, have your circumstances
caused you to rebel against God?

558
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:33,000
Maybe it's not an outward rebellion,
although that happens too.

559
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:38,000
We run from God, we pursue other things,
we go after our own desires.

560
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:42,000
But occasionally, these are inward
rebellions, where we start to doubt.

561
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:46,000
We start to question in such a way that
starts to become unhealthy.

562
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:51,000
We start to seek after different things,
and we begin, inside of our own hearts,

563
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:57,000
we begin to rebel almost exactly like the
three rebellions that we saw in Numbers.

564
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Maybe you're like the scouts in Numbers
chapter 13,

565
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:04,000
where they had a fear of what was out
there,

566
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:08,000
and a lack of trust that God would take
care of them.

567
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Or perhaps like Korah from Numbers 16,

568
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:16,000
where they allowed pride and jealousy to
consume them,

569
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:21,000
to go after their leaders and to put
themselves in their place.

570
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Or maybe you're like Moses and Aaron,

571
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:30,000
where you look at your life, and you are
taking credit for God's activity.

572
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:35,000
That bank account, your job, you look at
the things in which you have in your life,

573
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:38,000
and you think you are the one who created
those things.

574
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Where are you most susceptible for
rebellion?

575
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:48,000
Because of Jesus, our rebellion does not
lead to punishment,

576
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:50,000
and I'm so grateful for that.

577
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:53,000
When you and I approach God with humility,

578
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:55,000
when we confess our rebellion,

579
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:59,000
we remind ourselves that He is God, and we
are not.

580
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:03,000
Then we are reminded that it's on that
confession of faith

581
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:06,000
that we are standing on the rock that is
Jesus.

582
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:11,000
He is our foundation. He is our provider,
our sustainer.

583
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:16,000
He is our King. Amen and Amen.

584
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:18,000
I am so grateful for you.

585
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:23,000
This is a chance where you and I get to
sing to our King Jesus,

586
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:25,000
the one on which we stand.
